{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"arrays","title":"Arrays","group":"Arrays & Objects","order":21,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Arrays are ordered, zero-indexed, dynamically sized lists that can hold any mix of values. Under the hood they are objects with numeric keys and a magic <code>length</code>.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-plus\"></i>Creating arrays</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const a = [1, \"two\", { three: 3 }, [4]];\nconsole.log(a, a.length);\nconsole.log(Array.of(7), Array(3), Array(3).fill(0));\nconsole.log(Array.from(\"abc\"), Array.from({ length: 4 }, (_, i) =&gt; i * i));\nconsole.log([...\"hi\"], Array.from(new Set([1, 1, 2])));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>[ 1, 'two', { three: 3 }, [ 4 ] ] 4\n[ 7 ] [ &lt;3 empty items&gt; ] [ 0, 0, 0 ]\n[ 'a', 'b', 'c' ] [ 0, 1, 4, 9 ]\n[ 'h', 'i' ] [ 1, 2 ]</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p><code>Array(3)</code> creates 3 <em>holes</em> (empty slots), not 3 <code>undefined</code>s — and <code>map</code> skips holes. Use <code>Array.from({ length: 3 }, fn)</code> or <code>Array(3).fill(x)</code>.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrows-left-right\"></i>Adding and removing</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Where</th><th>Mutates?</th><th>Returns</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>push(x)</code> / <code>pop()</code></td><td>End</td><td>Yes</td><td>new length / removed item</td></tr><tr><td><code>unshift(x)</code> / <code>shift()</code></td><td>Start (O(n))</td><td>Yes</td><td>new length / removed item</td></tr><tr><td><code>splice(i, n, ...items)</code></td><td>Anywhere</td><td>Yes</td><td>array of removed items</td></tr><tr><td><code>slice(i, j)</code></td><td>Copy a range</td><td>No</td><td>new array</td></tr><tr><td><code>concat(...arrs)</code></td><td>Join</td><td>No</td><td>new array</td></tr><tr><td><code>toSpliced</code>, <code>with(i, v)</code></td><td>Copying variants (ES2023)</td><td>No</td><td>new array</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const arr = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"];\narr.push(\"e\");\nconst last = arr.pop();\narr.unshift(\"z\");\nconst first = arr.shift();\nconsole.log(arr, last, first);\n\nconst removed = arr.splice(1, 2, \"X\", \"Y\", \"Z\");   // at 1: remove 2, insert 3\nconsole.log(arr, removed);\nconsole.log(arr.slice(1, 3), arr.slice(-2), arr.with(0, \"!\"), arr[0]);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>[ 'a', 'b', 'c', 'd' ] e z\n[ 'a', 'X', 'Y', 'Z', 'd' ] [ 'b', 'c' ]\n[ 'X', 'Y' ] [ 'Z', 'd' ] [ '!', 'X', 'Y', 'Z', 'd' ] a</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-ruler\"></i><code>length</code> is writable</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const nums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];\nnums.length = 2;                 // truncates\nconsole.log(nums);\nnums[5] = 6;                     // creates holes\nconsole.log(nums, nums.length);\nconsole.log(nums.at(-1), nums[nums.length - 1]);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>[ 1, 2 ]\n[ 1, 2, &lt;3 empty items&gt;, 6 ] 6\n6 6</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-checks\"></i>Checking and converting</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>console.log(Array.isArray([]), typeof []);\nconsole.log([1, [2, 3]].toString(), String([null, undefined, 1]));\nconsole.log([3, 1, 2].join(\" &lt; \"), \"a-b-c\".split(\"-\"));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>true object\n1,2,3 ,,1\n3 &lt; 1 &lt; 2 [ 'a', 'b', 'c' ]</code></pre></figure>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>How do you empty an array?</summary><div><p><code>arr.length = 0</code> (mutates — every reference sees an empty array), <code>arr.splice(0)</code> (mutates, returns the removed items), or <code>arr = []</code> (rebinds only this variable; other references keep the old contents).</p></div></details></section>"}